&lt;li&gt;Identifying and securing strategic partnerships with trusted, well-known brands that create meaningful value for our paying customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading commercial negotiations and contract discussions with new and existing partners, building long-lasting, mutually beneficial relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scaling and optimising existing partnerships through data-driven insights, performance tracking and continuous improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analysing customer behaviour and commercial performance to identify the highest-impact partnership opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building strong relationships across Product, Marketing, Data Science, Design and Operations to seamlessly bring partnerships to life&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing partnerships from initial idea through implementation, optimisation and long-term success&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🤩 We’d love to hear from you if…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have a proven track record in partnerships, business development or growth, ideally within banking, fintech or technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You have experience building and scaling B2B and B2C partnerships that deliver measurable commercial and customer impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You&#39;re highly analytical and confident using data to inform decisions, identify opportunities and influence strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re an excellent communicator and relationship builder who can collaborate effectively with both internal stakeholders and external partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You enjoy working cross-functionally and can navigate technical, commercial and operational challenges with confidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’re excited by Monzo’s mission to make money work for everyone and want to help build products customers genuinely love&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Not ticking every box? That’s totally okay! Studies show that women and people of colour might hesitate to apply unless they meet every single requirement. At Monzo, we’re dedicated to creating a diverse and welcoming team. If you’re passionate about this role and keen to learn and grow with us, we encourage you to apply— even if you don’t have everything that&#39;s listed just yet. Drop us your application, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🙌 What’s in it for you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;💰 £86,000 - £115,000 ➕ Incentive Awards tied to your performance&lt;br&gt;📍This role is based in our London office&lt;br&gt;⏰ We offer flexible working hours and trust you to work enough hours to do your job well, and at times that suit you and your team.&lt;br&gt;📚 £1,000 learning budget each year to use on books, training courses and conferences.&lt;br&gt;🏡 We will set you up to work from home; all employees are given Macbooks and for fully remote workers we will provide extra support for your work-from-home setup.&lt;br&gt;➕ Plus lots more! &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/careers&quot;&gt;Read our full list of benefits.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;🌈 The application journey has 3 key steps&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruiter Call (30 minutes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initial Hiring Manager Call (30 minutes)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 hours of technical and behavioural interviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This process should take around 4-5 weeks - your schedule is really important to us, so we promise to be as flexible as possible!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have some guidelines on using Artificial Intelligence (AI) to ace an application and interview at Monzo. &lt;a href=&quot;https://monzo.com/blog/the-ultimate-guide-on-using-ai-to-ace-an-interview-at-monzo&quot;&gt;You can read them here.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
